{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794442361,"nonce":"8rFb2RuL9LmYcXSiG3dJV3KH2RM=","message":"Committed as e50b8fc, not pushed.\n\nWhat a result over time carries, beyond `()`, bool, `i32`, `f64`, text and an interface:\n\n- `i64`, by a future, a stream or a signal: `haxe.Int64` in Haxe, taken through `\u003clibrary\u003e_\u003ckind\u003e_take_long` (`next_long`, `get_long`), an `int64_t` over the C ABI and `l` in a HashLink signature.\n- `Vec\u003cu8\u003e`, by a future or a stream: `haxe.io.Bytes`. Over the C ABI the take writes a `Buf`, as a function returning bytes does; the HashLink primitive returns the VM's bytes and writes their length through a last `Ri` parameter. A signal does not carry bytes: it is read any number of times and bytes are handed over once.\n\nAn async function gives these by returning them.\n\nFixture: `Later::stamp`, `frame`, `frames`, `odometer`.\n\nStill not carried: the narrower numbers and `u64` (a carried type has no place for the Rust number beside what it crosses as), and an `Option`.\n\nRun: tests/counter/run.sh gen-hl on Ash (hybrid, jit, interp, three times each) and stock HashLink on the NUC, gen-cpp, gen-cppia, gen-wasm, gen-emcc, and the hand-written hl, cpp and emcc modes. Not run: Windows and hxcpp on Linux (CI on push), and the hand-written wasm mode, which the local Ash build traps in.","files":null}]}